
    Like-minded players can form teams with one another.  The team
leader, the player which forms the team, decides who can join and who
must leave.  Up to 8 players, including the leader, can be on a single
team.  Team members are able to keep in constant contact with one another,
regardless of location, through use of the team radio.
    The team score is a cumulative count of the scores of its members.
When points are added to a team member's score, the same number of points
are added to the team score.  Points gained prior to joining the team
(and any gained after leaving) are not added to the team's score.
    Teams may consider staking claim to a group of rooms, using the
claim from each team member to mark rooms as belonging to that team.
These rooms may then be used to store weapons or other items for other
members of the team to use at a later time.  Be forewarned!  If you use
your claim for your team and are ejected, the claim will remain the
property of the team and you WILL NOT get another.


Team commands:

 FORM <team_name>       Forms a new team with the indicated name with you
                        as the leader.
 DISBAND                Disbands your team.  You must be the leader to
                        disband a team.
 EJECT <player>         The team leader may eject an unwanted player from
                        the team ranks.
 RESIGN                 If you no longer want to be a part of the team,
                        you may resign.
 INVITE <player>        Offers the indicated player the opportunity to
                        join your team.  Only team leaders may invite
                        others to join the team.
 TEAM                   Lists players currently on your team and the team
                        score.
 LINE <message>         Sends the indicated message to all players on your
                        team currently in the game.
 ACCEPT                 Accepts the last offer received to join a team.
 DECLINE                Declines the last offer received to join a team.

